## Refined intent

**In scope:** change the **input RPE** the existing linear-decay formula sees. RPE 5 must produce a real e1RM **> load** for multi-rep sets. RPE below 5.0 uses the **same formula result as RPE 5.0**.

**Out of scope for the floor PR:** new %1RM tables, Brzycki/Epley, changing `RPE_CHART`, Insights client math, Sheets publish, Telegram. **The 25% cap is now in scope for the order PR** — see `e1rm-rpe-order.mdc`. Do not implement a floor-only PR that keeps the cap.

### Locked decisions

| Decision | Verdict | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Formula family | **Keep** linear decay `e1RM = weight / (1 - 0.03 * (10 - rpe + reps - 1))` | Canonical; do not invent a second formula. **No 25% cap** — `e1rm-rpe-order.mdc` |
| Floor | **`E1RM_RPE_FLOOR = 5.0`** (not 5.5, not 6.0) | User’s logged RPE **5** must run the formula at 5.0. 5.5 is a valid 0.5 step **above** the floor |
| 0.5 steps below 5 | **`0 < rpe < 5.0` → formula RPE = 5.0** | 4.5, 4.0, 3.5, … all equal RPE 5.0. Cleaner than “≤ 4” which would leave 4.5 as a hole |
| RPE 5.5 | **Use 5.5** (no clamp) | Half-step above the floor; linear decay is continuous |
| Missing RPE | **`rpe <= 0` still returns `weight`** (do **not** clamp 0 to 5) | Empty LOG RPE must not invent an e1RM as if it were RPE 5 |
| `reps > 12` | **Unchanged** — return `weight` | Independent reliability guard |
| Persist clamp? | **No.** Store the athlete’s 4.0. Clamp only the formula input | Numeric RPE stays the logged value |
| Which RPE is the input? | **Executed RPE** for the LOG e1RM column | `ExerciseCard` already uses `set.executedRpe`. Planned RPE is prescription, not the log projection. Backend may fall back to `plannedRpe` when executed is null — that value still goes through the same clamp |
| `MATH_VERSION` | Floor shipped **`linear-decay-v2`** on PR #19. Order PR bumps to **`linear-decay-v3`** | Do not keep v2’s capped 200.00 contract |
| 25% drop cap | **Drop** (superseded) | Cap flattens 150×6 @5 and @6 to 200, so @5 is not higher than @6. See `e1rm-rpe-order.mdc` |
| `RPE_CHART` / Helms table | **Do not add RPE 5 rows** | e1RM is linear decay, not a lookup. No new math libraries |

### Clamp (locked)

```text
if weight <= 0 or reps <= 0: return 0
if reps > 12: return weight
if rpe <= 0: return weight          # missing RPE ≠ RPE 5
formula_rpe = rpe if rpe >= 5.0 else 5.0
# drop math using formula_rpe — NO 25% cap (e1rm-rpe-order.mdc); denom guard; round 2 dp
```

Named constant in **both** engines: `E1RM_RPE_FLOOR = 5.0`. Do not leave a stray `6.0` on the e1RM path. Apply the same clamp in `calculateWeightFromE1RM`.

### Worked numbers (floor only — cap numbers superseded)

**Do not implement 200.00.** Live contract is `e1rm-rpe-order.mdc`: uncapped drop `0.03 * (10 - formula_rpe + reps - 1)`.

| weight | reps | logged RPE | formula RPE | e1RM (order / v3) | obsolete v2 (capped) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: |
| 150 | 6 | 5.0 | 5.0 | **214.29** (UI 214) | 200.00 |
| 150 | 6 | 6.0 | 6.0 | **205.48** (UI 205) | 200.00 |
| 150 | 6 | 7.0 | 7.0 | **197.37** (UI 197) | 197.37 |
| 150 | 6 | 4.0 | 5.0 | **214.29** == @5 | 200.00 |
| 150 | 6 | 0 / null | — | **150.00** | 150.00 |
| 100 | 5 | 5.5 | 5.5 | **134.23** | 133.33 |
| 100 | 3 | 5.0 / 5.5 / 4.0 | 5 / 5.5 / 5 | **126.58 / 124.22 / 126.58** | same (uncapped) |

